From b3a68d63d1b2a6174b23ab78ec068345a7df526f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:23:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(3d): rapid to the plunge height before a pocket
 restart, merge sub-resolution feeds

A 3D Pocket pass that restarts after a hop with a straight plunge now
goes down by a rapid to the plunge height over the material, then
feeds the rest (descent::feed_down, as a level entry does). Before, it
fed the whole way from the hop plane.

The finished 3D Pocket path merges each straight feed that moves less
than 0.001 mm on every axis into its straight neighbour. Such a move
posted as a G01 with the same X, Y and Z as the block before it.

The catalog case 3d/rough-finish is made again: 28 sub-resolution
G01 lines leave the 3D Pocket section.

Fixes #3852

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
